  "notes": "Supplied by Shlomi on 2026-10-08 as T1500.pdf. Bituach Leumi form בל/1500 (unemployment claim, 05.2026), PDF page 2 of 7, printed 'עמוד 1 מתוך 6' (pageIndex 1; page 1 is the instructions cover and has nothing to write): the header ID blank, section 1 (claimant details, marital status, children 18-24, addresses, phones, email, contact person, digital-notices consent) and section 2 (bank account). Flat Word export with a text layer, no AcroForm. Bounds are exact geometry, not eyeballed: ruled-cell interiors from a flood fill of the white regions of a 300 dpi render, comb ticks from the page's vector rects (collectPageInk as a geometry reader), underscore runs from the raster ink of the printed underscore glyphs, checkboxes from the ink of the ❑ glyph (10.08 pt square), then checked against the render with overlay.mjs. Conventions copied from btl-bl211-2015-page2 and -page7: tick combs are ONE target with cells (strip from the baseline to the regular tick tops, taller separator ticks excluded); a day/month/year tick comb is one date target (8 cells); a date on a blank underline is date, an ID or number on an underline is text; a plain underline is the 11 pt strip above the underscore run, as long as the run; a ruled cell that carries its caption inside (the name cells, the contact-person name cells) is bounded to the writing strip beneath the caption (caption baseline + 3.3 pt), a table input cell whose caption sits in a header row above is the whole interior and kind text, never table-cell; a checkbox is the printed square and single-choice groups (marital status, gender, account type, yes/no) are independent checkboxes, not radio; checkbox labels are the option word then ' / ' then the group caption or question, table-cell labels are the column caption then ' / ' then the table caption or row. New on this page: the email is two underlines either side of a printed @ and is annotated as two text targets; the three bank-owner name cells share one header caption and carry 'בעל חשבון N'; the repeated children rows carry a row number. Not annotated: the 'לשימוש פנימי בלבד' scan box (ID comb, document-type cells '0 0', pages cells), the 'חותמת קבלה' stamp box, the logo, the section badges, the grey section bars, the table header rows, the 'סוג החשבון' and 'מין' cells apart from their checkboxes, the bold 'נא לצרף אישור' notes and every pre-printed caption. Checkbox bounds are the printed square without the shadow (FORM-31 convention).",
